{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation detail for this story (the description carries the decisions).\n\nPair list for `tests/scripts/`, filtered from enumeration (2) of the test-suite epic's first comment. Format: `base | heldout LOC | RENAME (differing defs)`; the twin is `<base>_heldout.py`. No test-function name collides in these pairs; definitions that collide with DIFFERENT bodies are named in the RENAME column (rename on merge); every other colliding definition is identical (dedupe: keep the base copy; `pytestmark` counts here).\n\n| # | base | heldout LOC | RENAME (differing defs) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `tests/scripts/test_backfill_bug_class.py` | 134 | `_closed_bug` |\n| 2 | `tests/scripts/test_backfill_caused_by.py` | 127 | - |\n| 3 | `tests/scripts/test_backfill_complexity_clone.py` | 100 | `_repo_with_commits` |\n| 4 | `tests/scripts/test_canary_bridge.py` | 545 | `FakeRunner`, `alert_env`, `hb_env`, fixture `mod` |\n| 5 | `tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py` | 185 | `_SCRIPT`, `_adr`, fixture `gate` |\n| 6 | `tests/scripts/test_check_config_ownership.py` | 272 | `_root` |\n| 7 | `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads.py` | 343 | `_SCRIPT`, `_tree`, fixture `gate` |\n| 8 | `tests/scripts/test_migrate_success_criteria.py` | 206 | - |\n| 9 | `tests/scripts/test_normalize_ci_conclusion_port.py` | 188 | `_mod` |\n| 10 | `tests/scripts/test_run_reconcile_bridge.py` | 222 | - |\n\n10 pairs; 7 renames = rows 1, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 9. The held-out LOC for rows 5, 6 and 7 are the origin/main 083620b0 sizes; E10a-S3 (aware-obvious-sphinx) deletes from those three twins, before this story, the real-tree and CI-wiring tests named in table (3) of the test-suite epic's first comment (`test_check_adr_numbers_heldout.py`: `test_ci_wires_the_gate`, `test_real_repo_tree_is_clean`, `test_real_tree_has_no_duplicate_numbers`, `test_real_tree_marker_per_adr`, `test_real_check_script_runs_as_subprocess`; `test_check_config_ownership_heldout.py`: `test_real_source_tree_is_clean`, `test_main_on_real_tree_returns_zero`; `test_check_config_reads_heldout.py`: `test_real_repo_is_clean_with_default_paths`, `test_real_schema_markers_all_carry_pointers`, `test_string_read_fields_keep_their_marker_and_do_not_fire` (4 params), `test_the_real_schema_parks_no_markers_against_a_ticket`, `test_ci_wires_the_gate`), so this story merges the post-E10a-S3 remainder and takes its before-counts after that story landed.\n\nRename rule: suffix the HELD-OUT definition `_heldout` (e.g. `_closed_bug_heldout`, `_SCRIPT_HELDOUT` for a module constant, `gate_heldout` for a fixture, `FakeRunner_heldout` for a class) and repoint its callers; keep the base copy of identical definitions.\n\nMerge recipe per pair: `cat` the held-out module into the base under a `# ── held-out oracles (merged from <name>_heldout.py) ──` divider; keep the base module docstring and append the held-out docstring's \"what it proves\" paragraph (rows 5-7 keep their bug 2c58-e710-275e-4ff7 cite); dedupe identical definitions (incl. `pytestmark`); rename differing definitions with the `_heldout` suffix and repoint callers; `git rm` the held-out file. Record per pair: `pytest --collect-only -q <base> <heldout>` before, `pytest --collect-only -q <base>` after.\n\nNot in this story: `tests/scripts/test_check_config_reads_red_proof.py` (the only `*_red_proof.py`; untouched), the 8 `tests/scripts/*_seam_clean_heldout.py` modules (deleted by E10a-S1), and the 4 unpaired `tests/scripts/` held-out modules (renamed in S5)."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788807556614699635,"uuid":"8764b272-b982-4ce5-8342-9e66fc966c14"}